  "theorem": "For any Dirichlet character chi mod N with root-of-unity values and integer k>=1, N*P_k*B_{k,chi} is an algebraic integer, where P_k is the product of all rational primes <=k+1. Proof: expand B_k(a/N), then N*B_{k,chi}=sum_a chi(a) sum_{j=0}^k binom(k,j)B_j*a^(k-j)*N^j; von Staudt-Clausen implies P_k B_j integer for j<=k, chi(a) algebraic integer. This is denominator integrality, not a Selmer-length bound.",
  "limitation": "Finite tests use primitive nontrivial characters of prime modulus only; proof applies more broadly provided chi values are roots of unity."
}
